bound-lock/1 about="{count} lines are conjectures: nothing rests on them, and each names what would break it." at=witness:the-root-spoke-for-the-place by=owner epoch=1 form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/open/lead sig="ed25519:era1:xH5gwFNGnC4wzuBc4aE5DqjGOcx+zeASKSY3Y1/d+xiZlwFw/1q4hHczBxK4PevmnnItT1Kaeojo++M4xauZDw==" value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="The theory here is not an application of an algebra to a problem. It is one algebra, of a cell with two marks, and three theories that turn out to be that algebra seen from different sides: constraints with a price, states on a scale, and points with an epoch and an origin.\n\nWhat it proves is that the price of a fold, the freedom of a system in bits, the four states a verdict can hold, the spectrum a domain admits, the metric that shared observation induces and the phase an epoch carries are all consequences of the same lines. Each law names the view that implements it, and each view is a folder of the source: what is proved in the field view runs in the field view, and a law no operation reaches is a law this package refuses to claim." at=witness:the-root-spoke-for-the-place by=owner epoch=1 form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/paper sig="ed25519:era1:jKij+PgJttDz3es4j1ZgZ6QdyJLFxZZ98BM0nWC+GSVNP17wxUiV5JH5e3bYILQmESefsDW0o/Ss6gJ6FXtbBg==" value=present
